EGL capability probes — the instruments that found the 2026-08-27 r38p1 defect.

WHY THESE EXIST
  The vendor tree ships a Mali driver lifted from another vendor's firmware.
  tools/mali_candidate_check.sh validates the BINARY (sdk, revision, allocator,
  DT_NEEDED subset, symbol resolution). None of that can see a runtime
  capability table, and r38p1 shipped publicly advertising
  EGL_RECORDABLE_ANDROID on ZERO configs. Every camera/video GL pipeline got
  zero matches from eglChooseConfig and died with EGL_BAD_CONFIG (0x3005).
  It emits no avc record either — property-read refusals are dontaudit'd
  (system/sepolicy/public/domain.te:146) — so no denial sweep can find it.

  ⇒ After ANY change to the GPU driver, run ../egl-config-check.sh.

  eglprobe    every EGLConfig with surface type, native visual, recordable,
              framebuffer_target, and whether an ES2/ES3 context can be made.
  eglchoose   eglChooseConfig with the attribute lists real apps use, showing
              how many configs match. Zero matches is the failure mode.
  ahbprobe    asks gralloc (via AHardwareBuffer) which format+usage pairs it
              supports — the control that proves whether a config the driver
              refuses is the driver's decision or gralloc's. In 2026-08-27 it
              was the driver's, which ruled out a gralloc/companion-lib
              transplant before anyone attempted one.

BUILD (host, needs an NDK; no tree or lunch required)
  On this build box the NDK is at
      /mnt/external_nvme/android-sdk/ndk/27.0.12077973        (r27, clang 18)
  CC=<ndk>/toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/linux-x86_64/bin/clang
  for f in eglprobe eglchoose ahbprobe; do
    $CC --target=aarch64-linux-android33 -O1 -o $f $f.c -ldl
  done

  They resolve EGL through dlopen/dlsym, so they run against whatever driver
  /vendor is serving and need no link-time dependency on it.

RUN
  adb push eglprobe /data/local/tmp/ && adb shell chmod 755 /data/local/tmp/eglprobe
  adb shell /data/local/tmp/eglprobe

  ../egl-config-check.sh finds the binary here automatically. It compares
  CAPABILITY TOTALS against the stock baseline as a FLOOR -- more configs than
  stock is a pass, fewer is the 2026-08-27 defect. Set EGL_SHOW_DIFF=1 for the
  row-level diff, which is informational only: IDs renumber between driver
  generations, and diffing them row by row failed a perfectly good r54p1.

⚠ Run as an APP if you are testing property visibility. These run as shell/root,
  which CAN read vendor_default_prop; app domains cannot. That difference is the
  entire second half of the 2026-08-27 bug and a probe run as root will not show
  it. Use the app's own crash as the app-domain measurement.
